  "deviations": [
    "Text under 17px is raised to 17px, so the harness renders the artboard the same way.",
    "Headings 'In the record that day' and 'Not known when this arrived' keep the pack-neutral words; the canvas names the clinician's role, which must come from the pack.",
    "The line under the title has no clinician or way of seeing (no API field); it reads 'Linked to' and the question chips.",
    "'Show what came later (n)' sits beside the first card's title and wraps under it; the canvas has no such control (later entries are reached with the switch).",
    "'Change when this arrived' is shown only to the named expert; the mock is a viewer without that right, as the canvas draws it.",
    "'Change the day' sits in the foot between the two buttons, and 'Save note' sits at the right of the note card's last row; the canvas draws neither.",
    "The note's own-words label and the card hints are visually hidden (still read aloud); the canvas has no room for them.",
    "The back arrow in the foot is a 13px icon where the canvas uses a text arrow.",
    "Page numbers are not zero-padded (p.87, not p.087).",
    "The right-hand cards are not probed by box: their heights follow words the API does not carry (the first card is 3px taller for the later-entries control, which moves the cards below it by 3px).",
    "Hit areas are real boxes, not a ::after: every button and link is 52px tall as the 52px rule and the e2e check measure it. Links keep the board's text position (padding that a negative margin takes back); drawn chips and pills are taller than the board by the difference. Probes: dictate differ in height/position only."
  ],
  "artboardCss": "section[aria-label='Record page'] > div:nth-child(2) > *{visibility:hidden}",
  "budget": 2.0,
  "budgetReason": "Words the API has no field for (the clinician and way of seeing line, 'Filed, no action recorded', 'Marked by you as not seen', long dates in the app's pack-neutral headings) and the 'Show what came later' control, which the canvas does not draw, push the right-hand cards a few pixels and change their text; every box is probed. Right-hand cards group entries by page and fold other-page entries (the page's tested behaviour), where the canvas lists them flat."
